    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 298.0,
      "end": 301.03,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "exponential is I omega. So we must"
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 301.04,
      "end": 304.87,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "evaluate the polomial at i omega."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 304.88,
      "end": 306.79,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "And this is the solution provided that"
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 306.8,
      "end": 309.189,
      "duration": 2.389,
      "text": "the polomial evaluated at i omega"
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 309.199,
      "end": 311.35,
      "duration": 2.151,
      "text": "doesn't vanish."
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 311.36,
      "end": 312.79,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "And in our case the characteristic"
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 312.8,
      "end": 317.59,
      "duration": 4.79,
      "text": "polomial p of s"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 321.99,
      "end": 322.0,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "we worked out already to be s^2 + 8."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 322.0,
      "end": 324.79,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "So this gives us a particular solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 324.8,
      "end": 332.07,
      "duration": 7.27,
      "text": "for zed which is 1 / i omega squared"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 332.08,
      "end": 335.67,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "+ 8 on the denominator."
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 335.68,
      "end": 337.35,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "We have e to the i omega on the"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 337.36,
      "end": 341.11,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "numerator"
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 344.79,
      "end": 344.8,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "and of course one over uh i omega^ 2 + 8"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 344.8,
      "end": 347.029,
      "duration": 2.229,
      "text": "becomes 1 over"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 347.039,
      "end": 353.909,
      "duration": 6.87,
      "text": "8 - omega^ 2"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 355.43,
      "end": 355.44,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "and we know we don't have a problem"
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 355.44,
      "end": 357.189,
      "duration": 1.749,
      "text": "because omega we were told in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 357.199,
      "end": 359.35,
      "duration": 2.151,
      "text": "problem is not equal to equal to"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 359.36,
      "end": 362.55,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "the<unk> of 8. So in this case we know"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 362.56,
      "end": 364.07,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "that the denominator is not going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 364.08,
      "end": 365.749,
      "duration": 1.669,
      "text": "vanish."
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 365.759,
      "end": 368.07,
      "duration": 2.311,
      "text": "Okay. And now what we need to do is just"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 368.08,
      "end": 369.99,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "take x"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 370.0,
      "end": 372.309,
      "duration": 2.309,
      "text": "for the particular solution to be the"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 372.319,
      "end": 378.629,
      "duration": 6.31,
      "text": "real part of zed"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 381.27,
      "end": 381.28,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "which is going to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 381.28,
      "end": 385.189,
      "duration": 3.909,
      "text": "the real part I'll write it out 8 -"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 385.199,
      "end": 388.469,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "omega^ 2"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 388.479,
      "end": 391.51,
      "duration": 3.031,
      "text": "cossine omega t"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 391.52,
      "end": 402.15,
      "duration": 10.63,
      "text": "plus i sin omega t"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 406.469,
      "end": 406.479,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "which gives us 1 8us"
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 406.479,
      "end": 408.55,
      "duration": 2.071,
      "text": "omega^ 2"
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 408.56,
      "end": 415.27,
      "duration": 6.71,
      "text": "cosine omega t."
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 417.909,
      "end": 417.919,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay. So the total solution, the general"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 417.919,
      "end": 420.39,
      "duration": 2.471,
      "text": "solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 420.4,
      "end": 421.51,
      "duration": 1.11,
      "text": "is going to be the sum of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 421.52,
      "end": 424.469,
      "duration": 2.949,
      "text": "homogeneous solution plus the particular"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 424.479,
      "end": 427.11,
      "duration": 2.631,
      "text": "solution."
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 427.12,
      "end": 430.309,
      "duration": 3.189,
      "text": "And in our case, that's going to be C1"
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 430.319,
      "end": 432.79,
      "duration": 2.471,
      "text": "cosine omega t"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 432.8,
      "end": 438.629,
      "duration": 5.829,
      "text": "plus c2 sin omega t"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 452.07,
      "end": 452.08,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "cosine omega t. Sorry, these should be"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 452.08,
      "end": 458.55,
      "duration": 6.47,
      "text": "roots."
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 472.469,
      "end": 472.479,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "and this is the general solution."
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 472.479,
      "end": 474.629,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "So we were asked also why is this"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 474.639,
      "end": 476.71,
      "duration": 2.071,
      "text": "sometimes called an undamped forced"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 476.72,
      "end": 479.27,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "oscillator? Well, it's undamped because"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 479.28,
      "end": 480.629,
      "duration": 1.349,
      "text": "in the differential equation there was"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 480.639,
      "end": 482.71,
      "duration": 2.071,
      "text": "no damping term. there was no term"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 482.72,
      "end": 485.189,
      "duration": 2.469,
      "text": "proportional to x dot. And then"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 485.199,
      "end": 486.79,
      "duration": 1.591,
      "text": "secondly, it's forced because we have a"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 486.8,
      "end": 488.23,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "forcing on the right hand side. We have"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 488.24,
      "end": 491.029,
      "duration": 2.789,
      "text": "an input function f which in this case"
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 491.039,
      "end": 493.99,
      "duration": 2.951,
      "text": "is cosine omega t which doesn't depend"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 494.0,
      "end": 496.71,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "on x and that forces the differential"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 496.72,
      "end": 498.39,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "equation."
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 498.4,
      "end": 500.71,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "Also note that the forcing term gives"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 500.72,
      "end": 503.029,
      "duration": 2.309,
      "text": "rise to part of the solution which is"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 503.039,
      "end": 505.11,
      "duration": 2.071,
      "text": "directly proportional"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 505.12,
      "end": 506.629,
      "duration": 1.509,
      "text": "uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 506.639,
      "end": 509.909,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "to uh the forcing. In fact, it has the"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 509.919,
      "end": 511.589,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "same frequency but a different"
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 511.599,
      "end": 513.829,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "amplitude."
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 513.839,
      "end": 516.469,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "Okay, so this concludes part A. Now for"
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 516.479,
      "end": 525.43,
      "duration": 8.951,
      "text": "part B,"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 527.91,
      "end": 527.92,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "we're asked uh to use the ERF to solve"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 527.92,
      "end": 532.47,
      "duration": 4.55,
      "text": "the differential equation x dot dot"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 535.03,
      "end": 535.04,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "plus 2x dot"
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 535.04,
      "end": 538.47,
      "duration": 3.43,
      "text": "+ 4x"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 550.23,
      "end": 550.24,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And again we can use the same trick. The"
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 550.24,
      "end": 551.91,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "right hand side isn't of the form e to"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 551.92,
      "end": 555.829,
      "duration": 3.909,
      "text": "the i t or sorry e to the i3t. But what"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 555.839,
      "end": 561.11,
      "duration": 5.271,
      "text": "we can do is we can write cosine 3t"
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 570.79,
      "end": 570.8,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And then solve the differential equation"
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 570.8,
      "end": 575.829,
      "duration": 5.029,
      "text": "z dot dot + 2 zed dot + 4"
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 575.839,
      "end": 580.87,
      "duration": 5.031,
      "text": "zed equals e to the i3t."
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 580.88,
      "end": 583.75,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "And then take uh take x equals the real"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 583.76,
      "end": 586.15,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "part of zed. And in this case, we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 586.16,
      "end": 594.389,
      "duration": 8.229,
      "text": "only looking for a particular solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 600.949,
      "end": 600.959,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "using the ERF. So it's one over the"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 600.959,
      "end": 604.79,
      "duration": 3.831,
      "text": "characteristic polomial evaluated at 3 *"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 604.8,
      "end": 607.35,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "e to i3t."
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 607.36,
      "end": 608.949,
      "duration": 1.589,
      "text": "And what's the characteristic polomial"
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 608.959,
      "end": 611.509,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "of this differential equation?"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 611.519,
      "end": 614.15,
      "duration": 2.631,
      "text": "Well, P of S"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 614.16,
      "end": 617.03,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "is going to be S^2"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 617.04,
      "end": 621.509,
      "duration": 4.469,
      "text": "+ 2 S + 4."
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 621.519,
      "end": 625.19,
      "duration": 3.671,
      "text": "Which means that P of 3 I"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 625.2,
      "end": 628.31,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "is going to be 3 I^ 2"
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 628.32,
      "end": 631.19,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "+ 2 * 3 I"
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 631.2,
      "end": 633.43,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "+ 4,"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 633.44,
      "end": 638.87,
      "duration": 5.43,
      "text": "which gives us -9 + 4 is -5"
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 638.88,
      "end": 643.67,
      "duration": 4.79,
      "text": "+ 6 I."
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 645.509,
      "end": 645.519,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And putting the pieces together, we end"
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 645.519,
      "end": 648.31,
      "duration": 2.791,
      "text": "up getting that X is equal to the real"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 648.32,
      "end": 650.069,
      "duration": 1.749,
      "text": "part"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 650.079,
      "end": 656.87,
      "duration": 6.791,
      "text": "of 1 over 5 + 6 I"
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 668.949,
      "end": 668.959,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "and we can expand we can expand out the"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 668.959,
      "end": 671.43,
      "duration": 2.471,
      "text": "numerator using Oilers's formula to get"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 671.44,
      "end": 676.31,
      "duration": 4.87,
      "text": "cosine 3T + I sin 3T"
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 676.32,
      "end": 679.99,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "and when the dust settles"
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 680.0,
      "end": 689.509,
      "duration": 9.509,
      "text": "I get 1 over 61. Let me check my notes."
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 693.03,
      "end": 693.04,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "- 5 cossine 3t"
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 693.04,
      "end": 699.11,
      "duration": 6.07,
      "text": "+ 6 sin 3t."
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 700.71,
      "end": 700.72,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So I'll let you work out this last step"
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 700.72,
      "end": 703.19,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "for yourself."
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 703.2,
      "end": 705.509,
      "duration": 2.309,
      "text": "Okay. And then lastly, what is the"
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 705.519,
      "end": 707.11,
      "duration": 1.591,
      "text": "natural angular frequency of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 707.12,
      "end": 709.509,
      "duration": 2.389,
      "text": "differential equation? Well, this is"
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 709.519,
      "end": 711.269,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "just some notation. We sometimes call"
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 711.279,
      "end": 713.99,
      "duration": 2.711,
      "text": "the natural angular frequency uh to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 714.0,
      "end": 716.23,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "the square root"
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 716.24,
      "end": 719.19,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "of the term proportional to x. So in"
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 719.2,
      "end": 721.269,
      "duration": 2.069,
      "text": "this case, the term two here uh comes in"
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 721.279,
      "end": 726.47,
      "duration": 5.191,
      "text": "as a damping term. The natural frequency"
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 726.48,
      "end": 728.629,
      "duration": 2.149,
      "text": "which is sometimes written as omega"
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 728.639,
      "end": 731.269,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "squared is always equal to this term"
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 731.279,
      "end": 733.35,
      "duration": 2.071,
      "text": "which is four."
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 733.36,
      "end": 735.35,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "So the natural frequency the natural"
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 735.36,
      "end": 737.43,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "angular frequency omega kn would be"
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 737.44,
      "end": 741.03,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "the<unk> of 4 which would be two."
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 741.04,
      "end": 743.35,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "Okay. So I'd just like to quickly recap."
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 743.36,
      "end": 745.67,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "We've taken a look at forced oscillators"
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 745.68,
      "end": 747.35,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "and we've computed their solutions using"
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 747.36,
      "end": 750.15,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "the erf. And one common trend uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 750.16,
      "end": 752.79,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "particularly when we have an oscillating"
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 752.8,
      "end": 756.069,
      "duration": 3.269,
      "text": "uh input a forcing term is to first"
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 756.079,
      "end": 758.15,
      "duration": 2.071,
      "text": "change the oscillating term into a"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 758.16,
      "end": 760.15,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "complex exponential"
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 760.16,
      "end": 763.509,
      "duration": 3.349,
      "text": "then compute uh a particular solution"
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 763.519,
      "end": 766.389,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "using the erf formula and then take the"
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 766.399,
      "end": 770.15,
      "duration": 3.751,
      "text": "real part of the the erf solution to"
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 770.16,
      "end": 773.35,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "recover a real solution to the od that"
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 773.36,
      "end": 775.269,
      "duration": 1.909,
      "text": "gives us the particular solution and"
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 775.279,
      "end": 777.43,
      "duration": 2.151,
      "text": "then in some cases we also have to add"
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 777.44,
      "end": 779.59,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "the homogeneous solution to it to get"
    },
    {
      "index": 229,
      "start": 779.6,
      "end": 782.949,
      "duration": 3.349,
      "text": "the full general solution to the OD."
    },
    {
      "index": 230,
      "start": 782.959,
      "end": 784.87,
      "duration": 1.911,
      "text": "Okay, so I'd like to conclude here and"
    },
    {
      "index": 231,
      "start": 784.88,
      "end": 788.16,
      "duration": 3.28,
      "text": "I'll see you next time."
    }
  ],
  "course": {
    "category": "Mathematics",
    "title": "Differential Equations",
    "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL64BDFBDA2AF24F7E"
  }
}